/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueActions.css`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueForm.css`\n\n**Key Implementation Details:**\n\n**CreateIssueModal.tsx**:\n- Manages modal state with Redux (`closeCreateIssueModal`)\n- Handles form submission with `submitting` state (line 37)\n- Implements Escape key handler (lines 59-68)\n- Handles overlay click to close (lines 123-127)\n- Shows success message with created issue identifier\n- Form data reset on modal open\n\n**CreateIssueForm.tsx**:\n- Manages multiple form fields (team, title, description, status, priority, assignee, labels, project, cycle, due date, parent issue)\n- Closes dropdowns on outside click (lines 131-141)\n- All fields use `data-testid` attributes for testing\n\n**CreateIssueActions.tsx**:\n- Contains \"Cancel\" and \"Create Issue\" buttons\n- Both buttons become disabled when `submitting={true}` (lines 15, 23)\n- Submit button shows \"Creating...\" text while submitting\n\n**CSS Implementation:**\n- Modal overlay: `create-issue-overlay` with fixed positioning and backdrop blur\n- Modal body: `create-issue-modal` with flex layout\n- Disabled button states: `opacity: 0.6` and `cursor: not-allowed`\n- Success state: `cim-success` displays created identifier\n\n### 5. Playwright Configuration\n**Path**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n\nConfiguration details:\n- Test timeout: 60 seconds\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- Using Replay Chromium devices\n- Reporter: Replay, JSON, and HTML\n- Action timeout: 15 seconds\n- Tests run fully in parallel\n\n### Test Data-TestIds Available for Tests\nThe components use consistent test IDs for easy selection:\n- `create-issue-modal-overlay` - The overlay/backdrop\n- `create-issue-modal` - The modal container\n- `create-issue-submit-btn` - Submit button\n- `create-issue-cancel-btn` - Cancel button\n- `create-issue-title-input` - Title field\n- And many others for form fields...\n\n### Testing Patterns Used\nFrom existing test file `create-issue-modal-form.spec.ts`:\n- Helper functions for login and navigation\n- API-based authentication\n- Token stored in localStorage\n- Waiting for elements with timeout\n- Testing disabled button states\n- Checking modal visibility\n\nAll four test areas you need are well-supported by the existing component implementation and can be written following the established patterns in the existing test files."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ae883241d003ec144 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 50425\ntool_uses: 24\nduration_ms: 33613</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54681ede-564a-4d83-857e-e1c1fbe67772","uuid":"50ba5075-56a1-4adc-89f1-ce566a97ef70","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to find the app related to a \"linear clone\" project. Look for:\n1. The app directory under /repo/apps/ - find which app this is\n2. The docs/tests.md file within the app directory that contains test specs\n3. Any existing test files (*.spec.ts) in the app\n4. The playwright config file\n5. Look for any modal/create issue related components\n\nBe thorough - I need to understand the app structure for writing tests about:\n- Create Issue button disabled during submission\n- Clicking outside modal closes it\n- Pressing Escape closes modal\n- Creating multiple issues in sequence","agentId":"ae883241d003ec144","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I now have a comprehensive understanding of the LinearClone project. Let me create a clear summary of my findings:\n\n## LinearClone Project Structure Summary\n\n### App Location\nThe linear clone project is located at `/repo/apps/LinearClone/`\n\n### 1. App Directory Structure\n```\n/repo/apps/LinearClone/\n├── src/\n│   ├── components/\n│   ├── pages/\n│   ├── slices/\n│   ├── store.ts\n│   ├── App.tsx\n│   ├── main.tsx\n│   └── index.css\n├── tests/\n├── netlify/\n├── docs/\n│   └── tests.md\n├── AppSpec.md\n├── playwright.config.ts\n├── package.json\n└── [build/config files]\n```\n\n### 2. Documentation File\n**Path**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md` (48,070 lines)\n\nThis file contains comprehensive test specifications including the specific test cases you need:\n- **Line 1426-1429**: \"Create Issue button is disabled during submission\"\n- **Line 1431-1434**: \"Clicking outside the modal closes it\" \n- **Line 1436-1439**: \"Pressing Escape closes the modal\"\n- **Line 1441-1444**: \"Creating multiple issues in sequence works correctly\"\n\n### 3. Existing Test Files\nMultiple test spec files exist in `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/`:\n- `create-issue-modal-form.spec.ts` - Form field rendering tests (already has 98-246 lines)\n- `create-issue-modal-selectors.spec.ts`\n- `create-issue-modal-cycles-dates.spec.ts`\n- `create-issue-modal-actions-integration.spec.ts` - Starts at line 83 with action tests\n\n### 4. Modal/Create Issue Components\n\n**Primary Component Files:**\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueModal.tsx` (173 lines)\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueForm.tsx` (603 lines)\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueActions.tsx` (31 lines)\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueModal.css`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueActions.css`\n- `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueForm.css`\n\n**Key Implementation Details:**\n\n**CreateIssueModal.tsx**:\n- Manages modal state with Redux (`closeCreateIssueModal`)\n- Handles form submission with `submitting` state (line 37)\n- Implements Escape key handler (lines 59-68)\n- Handles overlay click to close (lines 123-127)\n- Shows success message with created issue identifier\n- Form data reset on modal open\n\n**CreateIssueForm.tsx**:\n- Manages multiple form fields (team, title, description, status, priority, assignee, labels, project, cycle, due date, parent issue)\n- Closes dropdowns on outside click (lines 131-141)\n- All fields use `data-testid` attr